# Generated from: specs/620-install-issue-worktree-dependencies-through-worktree-setup-and-rerun-setup-when-it-never-ran-or-changed/requirements.md
Feature: Install issue worktree dependencies through worktree setup and rerun setup when it never ran or changed

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: This repository declares a dependency-installing setup
    Given this repository's "steering/manifest.json"
    When its optional settings are read and validated
    Then "worktree.setup" is the command "npm" with args "ci" and cwd "scripts"
    And validation does not fail

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A never-run setup runs on reuse
    Given an issue worktree created while no setup command was declared
    And its record shows setup succeeded without running a command
    And the worktree's manifest now declares a setup command
    When the worktree is reused
    Then the declared setup command runs once in the worktree
    And the record stores the result and the command that ran

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A changed setup command runs on reuse
    Given an issue worktree whose record shows a successful run of setup command A
    And the worktree's manifest now declares setup command B
    When the worktree is reused
    Then setup command B runs once
    And the record stores command B

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: An unchanged successful setup is not repeated
    Given an issue worktree whose record shows a successful run of the declared setup command
    When the worktree is reused with the same declaration
    Then setup does not run again
    And the record is unchanged

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Existing setup behavior is preserved
    Given a project that declares setup and teardown commands
    When a "spec/7-new-thing" worktree is created, reused and removed
    Then neither setup nor teardown runs for it
    And a failing setup on an issue worktree fails with "worktree_setup_failed" and runs again on the next reuse

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario Outline: The documentation describes when setup reruns
    Given the file "<file>"
    When its description of the worktree setup command is read
    Then it contains "On a reused issue worktree, setup runs again when the recorded setup failed, ran no command while one is now declared, or ran a different command than the one now declared."

    Examples:
      | file                          |
      | references/steering-schema.md |
      | README.md                     |
